      <t:body>
         <t:listPlace>
            <t:place type="church monastery gadam" subtype="institution">
               
               <t:placeName xml:id="n1" xml:lang="gez">መኾድዐ፡ ደብረ፡ ገነት፡ ኪዳነ፡ ምሕረት፡ </t:placeName>
               <t:placeName corresp="#n1" xml:lang="gez" type="normalized">Maḵodʿa Dabra Gannat Kidāna Mǝḥrat</t:placeName>
               <t:placeName xml:lang="gez" xml:id="n2">ደብረ፡ ገነት፡ ኪዳነ፡ ምሕረት፡ መኾድዐ፡</t:placeName>
               <t:placeName type="normalized" xml:lang="gez" corresp="#n2">Dabra Gannat Kidāna Mǝḥrat Maḵodʿa</t:placeName>

               
               
               <t:country ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC3010Ethiop">Ethiopia</t:country>
               <t:region notBefore="1991" type="RegionalState" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC5932Tegray">Bǝḥerāwi Kǝllǝlāwi Mangǝśti Tǝgrāy</t:region>
               
               <t:settlement type="warada" when="2010-12-04" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC3293GantaA">Gāntā ʾAfašum</t:settlement>
               <t:settlement type="tabiya" when="2010-12-04" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC7220Gullat">Gullāt</t:settlement>
               <t:settlement type="qushat" when="2010-12-04" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC7221Makoda">Maḵodʿa</t:settlement>
            

               <t:location>
                  <t:geo>14.189278 39.362222</t:geo>
                  <t:height unit="m">2370.0</t:height>
               </t:location>
               <t:note>
                  <t:date type="foundation" notBefore="1600" notAfter="1600">1600-1600</t:date>
                  <t:desc type="foundation">Possibly diring the time of <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS6229LebnaDe">King Lǝbnā Dǝngǝl</t:persName> (r. <t:date>1508-1540</t:date>), re-established late 17th or early 18th cent. 
                     <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS6951Mazgaba">Mazgaba Śǝllāse</t:persName>, the late 17th - early 18th-cent. head of Gunda Gunde, played a role in the establishement of the local monastic community.</t:desc>
                  <t:ab type="history">Gadam. Some 10 monks were residing in the monastery at the time of the visit. 
                     </t:ab>
                  <t:ab type="description">
                     <t:figure>
                        <t:graphic url="Sites/GKM.tif">
                           <t:desc>The church photographed by Denis Nosnitsin during the Ethio-SPaRe project.</t:desc>
                        </t:graphic>
                     </t:figure>
                     22 Mss. photographed: <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESgkm001">GKM-001</t:ref> "The Spiritual Elder"; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESgkm002">GKM-002</t:ref> "Miracles of Mary"; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESgkm003">GKM-003</t:ref> "The Book of the Chants"; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESgkm004">GKM-004</t:ref> "Miracles of Mary"; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESgkm005">GKM-005</t:ref> "Four Gospels"; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESgkm006">GKM-006</t:ref> "The Rite of the Holy Week"; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESgkm007">GKM-007</t:ref> "Homily of the Living One"; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESgkm008">GKM-008</t:ref> "Pauline Epistles"; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESgkm009">GKM-009</t:ref> "Synaxarion (September)"; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESgkm010">GKM-010</t:ref> "The Book of the Funeral Rite"; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESgkm011">GKM-011</t:ref> "Synaxarion (March)"; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESgkm012">GKM-012</t:ref> "Miracles of Mikaʾel"; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESgkm013">GKM-013</t:ref> "Vita of Mäzgäbä Śǝllase"; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESgkm014">GKM-014</t:ref> "Psalter"; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESgkm015">GKM-015</t:ref> "Prayer of Incense"; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESgkm016">GKM-016</t:ref> "Miracles of Jesus"; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESgkm017">GKM-017</t:ref> "The Covenant of Mary"; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESgkm018">GKM-018</t:ref> "Psalter"; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESgkm019">GKM-019</t:ref> "Collection of Maryam Texts and hymns"; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESgkm020">GKM-020</t:ref> "Prayers of Mary"; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESgkm021">GKM-021</t:ref> "The Book of the Baptismal Rite; The Book of the Baptismal Rite"; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESgkm022">GKM-022</t:ref> fragments of a Missal and a Psalter.</t:ab>
                  <t:ab type="tabot"> 
                     <t:measure quantity="44"/>   Tābots: said to be "44", i.e. very many, both wooden and marble; specifically were mentioned tābots of 
                     <t:persName type="tabot" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS10775Trinity">Trinity</t:persName>, <t:persName type="tabot" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS6951Mazgaba">Mazgaba Śǝllāse</t:persName>, 
                     <t:persName type="tabot" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS7049Michael">Michael</t:persName>, <t:persName type="tabot" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS5684JesusCh#n3MadhaneAlam">Madḫāne ʿĀlam</t:persName>, <t:persName type="tabot" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS6819Mary">Mary</t:persName>.  
                     Possibly there exists also specifically <t:ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/CovenantMercy">Kidāna Mǝḥrat</t:ref>.
</t:ab>               
               </t:note>
            </t:place>
         </t:listPlace>
